---
---
<section id="problem" class="py-24 px-6 border-t border-[var(--border)] relative bg-[var(--bg-base)]">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-16">
      <div class="page-tag">
        // SYSTEM_FAILURE_DETECTED
      </div>
      <h2 class="page-heading text-3xl md:text-5xl">Why Other ML Courses Don't Work</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <!-- Card 1 -->
      <div class="lift p-6 rounded-lg relative overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--bg-surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <svg class="w-8 h-8 mb-4 text-[var(--purple-dim)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M2.458 12C3.732 7.943 7.523 5 12 5c4.478 0 8.268 2.943 9.542 7-1.274 4.057-5.064 7-9.542 7-4.477 0-8.268-2.943-9.542-7z" />
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Video courses are passive</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          Watching someone else code feels productive, but you forget 90% of it in 72 hours. You need to write the code yourself to build neural pathways.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2 -->
      <div class="lift p-6 rounded-lg relative overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--bg-surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <svg class="w-8 h-8 mb-4 text-[var(--purple-dim)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10" />
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Toy projects don't scale</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          Classifying the Titanic dataset doesn't prepare you for real AI pipelines, RAG implementations, or deploying models to production.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3 -->
      <div class="lift p-6 rounded-lg relative overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--bg-surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <svg class="w-8 h-8 mb-4 text-[var(--purple-dim)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M8 12h.01M12 12h.01M16 12h.01M21 12c0 4.418-4.03 8-9 8a9.863 9.863 0 01-4.255-.949L3 20l1.395-3.72C3.512 15.042 3 13.574 3 12c0-4.418 4.03-8 9-8s9 3.582 9 8z" />
        </svg>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Zero feedback loop</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          When you get stuck, you're on your own. You never know if your solution is optimal or if you just hacked it together until it worked.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
